c{(y-7)^{2}}{6} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(-6,7).$" 13194139533892 true] [17592186083476 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533892 true] [17592186083476 1145 "The equation of a horizontal hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}{x}^{2}-5{y}^{2}+2x+10y & =9 \\\\ {x}^{2}+2x-5{y}^{2}+10y & =9 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}-1-5[{y}^{2}-2y] & =9 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}-1-5[(y-1)^{2}-1] & =9 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}-1-5(y-1)^{2}+5 & =9 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}-5(y-1)^{2} & =9+1-5 \\\\ (x+1)^{2}-5(y-1)^{2} & =5 \\\\ \\frac{(x+1)^{2}}{5}-(y-1)^{2} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nTherefore, the center is $(-1,1).$" 13194139533892 true] [17592186263977 1017 #edb/ref 17592186263978 13194139533892 true] [17592186263977 1089 "q-10419" 13194139533892 true] [17592186263977 1091 #edb/ref 17592186045465 13194139533892 true] [17592186263977 1100 "What is the center of the hyperbola $4{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}-16y+4x=0?$" 13194139533892 true] [17592186263977 1113 #uuid "70a4a2a9-00d7-57b7-8107-169920caa030" 13194139533892 true] [17592186263977 1145 "The equation of a vertical hyperbola centered at $(h,k)$ is given by\n\n$$\n\\frac{(y-k)^{2}}{{a}^{2}}-\\frac{(x-h)^{2}}{{b}^{2}}=1.\n$$\n\nTo rewrite the equation of the hyperbola in the above form, we need to group $x$ and $y$ terms and complete the squares, as follows:\n\n$$\n\\begin{aligned}4{y}^{2}-{x}^{2}-16y+4x & =0 \\\\ 4{y}^{2}-16y-{x}^{2}+4x & =0 \\\\ 4[{y}^{2}-4y]-[{x}^{2}-4x] & =0 \\\\ 4[(y-2)^{2}-4]-[(x-2)^{2}-4] & =0 \\\\ 4(y-2)^{2}-16-(x-2)^{2}+4 & =0 \\\\ 4(y-2)^{2}-(x-2)^{2} & =16-4 \\\\ 4(y-2)^{2}-(x-2)^{2} & =12 \\\\ \\frac{(y-2)^{2}}{3}-\\frac{(x-2)^{2}}{12} & =1.\\end{aligned}\n$$\n\nHence, the center is $(2,2).$" 13194139533892 true] [17592186263978 1000 #edb/ref 17592186263979 13194139533892 true] [17592186263978 1000 #edb/ref